        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "843959ad-6784-51ab-bacc-03ddd58a25cb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Marilyn Buck, Assata Shakur, Werner Foerster\n- Organizations: Black Liberation Army\n- Events: 1973 New Jersey Turnpike shootout, 1977 murder conviction, 1979 prison escape, 1981 Brink's robbery, 1983 U.S. Senate bombing\n- Topics: Marxist revolutionary activism, feminist poetry, black nationalist urban guerrilla activity\n\nFacts:\n- Marilyn Buck was born on December 13, 1947, and she died on August 3, 2010.\n- Assata Shakur was born JoAnne Deborah Byron on July 16, 1947, and is often referred to by her married surname Chesimard.\n- Assata Shakur was a former member of the Black Liberation Army, a black nationalist urban guerrilla group.\n- In 1973, Werner Foerster was killed during a shootout on the New Jersey Turnpike.\n- In 1977, Assata Shakur was convicted of the first-degree murder of Werner Foerster under New Jersey's aiding and abetting statute.\n- In 1979, Marilyn Buck participated in the prison escape of Assata Shakur.\n- In 1981, Marilyn Buck participated in the Brink's robbery.\n- In 1983, Marilyn Buck participated in the U.S. Senate bombing.\n- Marilyn Buck was an American Marxist revolutionary and feminist poet who was imprisoned for her participation in those actions.",
